  "title": "Clean UNIT_DATA membership residue and retire JULIA_COMPUTE registration",
  "summary": "Human-governor finding 2026-10-02: two current residues in project_architecture_directory. (1) UNIT_DATA responsibilities still declares 'members:POSTGRESQL_AUTHORITY|QDRANT_AUTHORITY|module-sqlite|local-vector|ollama' - module-sqlite and ollama have no directory rows and do not parent to UNIT_DATA, local-vector (LOCAL_VECTOR) parents to UNIT_PLATFORM, so the declared membership diverges from the actual parent_code linkage (POSTGRESQL_AUTHORITY + retired QDRANT_AUTHORITY). The members list is corrected to the two rows that actually parent to UNIT_DATA; the retired member is retained consistent with the directory convention (UNIT_ASSISTANT retains STAR_DIRECTORY, UNIT_RUNTIME retains SUB_SOVEREIGN_LAYER, UNIT_ENGINE retains MODEL_TRAINING). (2) JULIA_COMPUTE is registered as an active internal-service although the current core language pool (B166 PRIMARY-CORE-LANGUAGE-POOL: C+C++23+CSharp+Rust+Go+FSharp only) no longer includes Julia - the entry has no authorized current owner. It is retired: entity_kind becomes retired-former-scientific-compute-service and retired_version binds to the successor codex version (same retirement shape as MODEL_TRAINING/QDRANT_AUTHORITY). The a233_normalized_directory_entry rows are updated in the same revision so canonical and projection do not diverge; JULIA_COMPUTE's a233 domain_payload embed is synced in a follow-up amendment once the concrete successor version is known (the embedded JSON string cannot carry the <successor-version> sentinel). Codex-only change: no implementation is modified.",
  "requested_by": "decision-sovereign",
  "origin": "direct human-governor finding 2026-10-02: UNIT_DATA still lists QDRANT_AUTHORITY|module-sqlite|local-vector|ollama as members; JULIA_COMPUTE is registered as an active internal service although B166 core language pool is C/C++23/CSharp/Rust/Go/FSharp and the latest language projection has no Julia current owner.",
